  "details": "For as long as I've been able to access the community through VR, I've used an Oculus Quest 1 (bought to be used by the family) Linked through USB to my PC to run PC games. I run the PC Version through the Quest headset.\nProblem is, with this new EAC malware (I do not use that term lightly) installed on my PC through VRC, I cannot use Oculus Link's in-headset features to control my PC. Which means I can no longer get into Discord calls, no longer have immediate access to Firefox when I need it, no more copy and pasting music links into in-game music players. And to top it off, even after I close the game, I do not regain control in-headset until I restart my PC. To say I'm upset would be a huge understatement, just saying. \nPlease, for the love of god VRC, listen to the community of your community-based program. This should not be an issue, especially when the entire community has voiced their opinion.",
